<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan stock exchange closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistan stock exchange closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) was closed on Wednesday due to a national holiday to observe the 48th anniversary of the death of Pakistan's founder Mohammad Ali Jinnah, KSE officials said.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the KSE 100-share-index fell 19.87 points, or 1.47 percent to close at 1,332.14 with 151 losers and 55 gainers on turnover of 21.1 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
